WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.203
- But first

00:00:01.203 --> 00:00:03.720
I want you to meet Morgan
Harper Nichols, everybody.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.150
She is an amazing poet.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:06.720
Look at that hat and that little, okay.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.500
She looks so cute in that picture too.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.550
She is an amazing poet

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:12.900
a musician and artist
whose social media presence

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.540
has earned the devotion of
millions, including celebrities

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.700
like Reese Witherspoon
and Jennifer Garner.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.330
Earlier this year, Morgan
announced she was autistic

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:23.760
and that sparked a conversation
on diagnosing autism

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.080
and adults, you know, hear
that, you know, as much.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.900
And so she's also out

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.860
with a new book called
how far you have come.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.170
Let's get her in here.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.223
What's up. Morgan Harper,
Nichols. How you doing?

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:37.910
- Hello? Hello.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.260
Thank you for having me.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.180
I'm doing well. Doing well.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.300
- Oh my God! You look great.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.900
I love the like handkerchief here.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:44.870
You're so cute.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.110
Yes, it's awesome.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.300
So you're a very successful artist

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.230
but until this diagnosis,
you really struggled, right?

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:56.230
- Yes. So I grew up struggling
with a lot of sensory issues

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.960
but I didn't know that's what they were.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.250
I would just feel overwhelmed in settings

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.570
with loud music or bright
lights, and I never knew why.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.690
And then I also struggled a lot

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:08.720
with making friends and social situations

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.120
with like even listening and
understanding tone of voice

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.790
but I didn't know what any of this was.

00:01:15.790 --> 00:01:18.780
And I spent my whole childhood

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.320
up until recently not knowing.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:24.840
So yeah, it's a bit of
how, how that came about.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.130
- I can only imagine how
that would have, you know

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:29.510
really crippled you socially,
you know, growing up

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:33.030
and not knowing how to, you
know, having any tools I guess

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.470
to get through that, those
emotions and those hardships.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.390
So is this true though, that

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.370
of TikTOK video led to your diagnosis?

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:41.740
- Yes, it was.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.700
I was on TikTOK and

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.300
for some reason the algorithm
decided to show me stories

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.930
like back to back stories

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.040
of women who had been diagnosed as adults.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:52.920
And I was like, wait a minute.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.190
I don't know anything
about this, but they saw

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:57.350
it sounds like they're
describing my whole life.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:02:00.630
So that is what gave
you the courage to get

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:03.450
on Google and find a
specialist in my area.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.090
And thankfully I was able to find someone.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.950
So yeah, that's what led me
to be able to get diagnosed.

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:13.130
- Wow. A TikTok who would
have thought that's amazing.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:14.660
So well, you have a new book?

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:17.880
And first I have to show
people how beautiful it is.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:20.110
It is just such a beautiful book.

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.960
I mean the art in it, like it's so pretty.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.190
So can you tell us about this?

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.130
Like what made you want to do this book?

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:29.550
- Yeah, so I am a visual
artist and a poet.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:33.410
And especially over this
past year, like many people

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.710
I haven't been able to do a lot

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.030
of the things that I love to do.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.620
I love to go places and see new things.

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:40.770
So art for me has been a way

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.270
of really just expressing gratitude

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:46.950
for what has been beautiful
about my story, what I have

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.980
how I have learned, how I have grown.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:49.950
And I just think

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:54.190
that we all need these moments
right now, more than ever

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.590
of just having gratitude
for how far we've come.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:02:59.240
So I hope that the poetry and art

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.250
in this book can help
people reflect on that.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.830
- I love the message too, because a lot

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:05.930
of people would say how far we need to go.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.132
And I actually, my therapist
told me this recently TMI

00:03:09.132 --> 00:03:11.550
but it's like, I always focus on, Oh God

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:12.770
I still have to do
this. I have to do this.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.200
I really want.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.900
And she's like, why don't we
look at like, where you've come

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.690
from? Like, you know, like from this point

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.651
to this point, like, and
it's an amazing thing

00:03:19.651 --> 00:03:22.450
but I think a lot of us, some
of us might be perfectionist.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:26.970
So, but how far you have come
by Morgan Harper Nichols.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.610
Y'all it's out right now.

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:30.550
If you can't get yourself a physical copy.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:31.990
It is beautiful.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:33.350
Thank you so much, Morgan

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.940
for sharing your story with everybody.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.820
- Oh, well thank you for having me.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.653
Thank you.

